Highway Traffic Act, s. 134 – Direction of traffic by police officer (part 1 of 2)
(1) Where a police officer or an officer appointed for carrying out the provisions of this Act considers it reasonably necessary,
(a) to ensure orderly movement of traffic;
(b) to prevent injury or damage to persons or property; or
