Highway Traffic Act, s. 220 – Impounding motor vehicles (part 1 of 4)
(1) In conjunction with a conviction under section 47, 51 or 53 of this Act or section 320.14 or 320.15 of the Criminal Code (Canada) or with a second conviction under section 320.16 of the Criminal Code (Canada), an order may issue that the motor vehicle driven by or under the care, charge or control of the person convicted at the time of the commission of the offence or second offence, as the case may be, shall be seized, impounded and taken into custody of the law for three months, subject to the conditions and in the manner set out in the order.  ;
